The attached image, Fig. 5, demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel (A) dot plots show that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) or Nano-11 alone results in moderate uptake, co-incubation with Nano-11 adsorbed OVA leads to a substantial increase in both Nano-11 and OVA signals within cells, indicating efficient co-delivery and internalization. Panel (B) histogram further quantifies this, showing a prominent shift in FITC-OVA fluorescence intensity for BMDCs treated with Nano-11+OVA compared to OVA alone, confirming enhanced antigen uptake and delivery to antigen-presenting cells, a critical step for immune activation.